{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" function is a factory that can be used to create a file-based route instance. This route instance can then be used to automatically generate a route tree with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr generate"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr watch"},{"type":"text","value":" commands."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createfileroute-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createFileRoute options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a single argument of type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that represents the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" of the file that the route will be generated from."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"path-option","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" literal"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required, but "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"automatically inserted and updated by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr generate"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr watch"},{"type":"text","value":" commands"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full path of the file that the route will be generated from"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createfileroute-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createFileRoute returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new function that accepts a single argument of type "},{"type":"link","href":"./RouteOptionsType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RouteOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that will be used to configure the file "},{"type":"link","href":"./RouteType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instance."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ Note: For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr generate"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsr watch"},{"type":"text","value":" to work properly, the file route instance must be exported from the file using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"},{"type":"text","value":" identifier."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: () => {\n    return 'Hello World'\n  },\n  component: IndexComponent,\n})\n\nfunction IndexComponent() {\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"createfileroute-options","text":"createFileRoute options","level":2},{"id":"path-option","text":"path option","level":3},{"id":"createfileroute-returns","text":"createFileRoute returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `createFileRoute` function is a factory that can be used to create a file-based route instance. This route instance can then be used to automatically generate a route tree with the `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` commands.\n\n## createFileRoute options\n\nThe `createFileRoute` function accepts a single argument of type `string` that represents the `path` of the file that the route will be generated from.\n\n### `path` option\n\n- Type: `string` literal\n- Required, but **automatically inserted and updated by the `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` commands**\n- The full path of the file that the route will be generated from\n\n## createFileRoute returns\n\nA new function that accepts a single argument of type [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md) that will be used to configure the file [`Route`](./RouteType.md) instance.\n\n> ⚠️ Note: For `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` to work properly, the file route instance must be exported from the file using the `Route` identifier.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: () => {\n    return 'Hello World'\n  },\n  component: IndexComponent,\n})\n\nfunction IndexComponent() {\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createFileRouteFunction\ntitle: createFileRoute function\n---\n\nThe `createFileRoute` function is a factory that can be used to create a file-based route instance. This route instance can then be used to automatically generate a route tree with the `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` commands.\n\n## createFileRoute options\n\nThe `createFileRoute` function accepts a single argument of type `string` that represents the `path` of the file that the route will be generated from.\n\n### `path` option\n\n- Type: `string` literal\n- Required, but **automatically inserted and updated by the `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` commands**\n- The full path of the file that the route will be generated from\n\n## createFileRoute returns\n\nA new function that accepts a single argument of type [`RouteOptions`](./RouteOptionsType.md) that will be used to configure the file [`Route`](./RouteType.md) instance.\n\n> ⚠️ Note: For `tsr generate` and `tsr watch` to work properly, the file route instance must be exported from the file using the `Route` identifier.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  loader: () => {\n    return 'Hello World'\n  },\n  component: IndexComponent,\n})\n\nfunction IndexComponent() {\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}\n```\n"}
